# No Cursor or AI attribution

Never mention Cursor, Copilot, ChatGPT, or any AI assistant as the author, co-author, or source of work.

## Git commits

- Commit messages must look like a normal human developer wrote them.
- Do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any similar trailer.
- Do not write "Generated by Cursor", "Assisted by AI", or equivalent in the subject or body.
- If the environment would inject a Cursor co-author trailer, do not run `git commit`. Stage the files if asked, then tell the user to commit from their own terminal.

## Pull requests, comments, and code

- PR titles and bodies must not mention Cursor or AI.
- Do not add AI attribution in code comments, README, or changelog.
- Do not sign off as Cursor.

## Examples

```
# Bad
git commit -m "Fix auth WebView back.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>"

# Good
git commit -m "Fix auth WebView so the device back button closes sign-in."
```
